<title>USA: U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. soybean weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. soybean major sales activity in the week ended Oct 10 reported by exporters for the following purchasing countries, in tonnes:</p>
<p>Net Sales:  1996/97		     1997/98</p>
<p>Unknown     256,900			   Nil</p>
<p>Netherlands 172,800</p>
<p>China	 100,000</p>
<p>Mexico	 80,500</p>
<p>Taiwan	 76,000-A</p>
<p>Brazil	 60,000</p>
<p>A-includes 38,000 in new sales and 38,000 in destination changes.</p>
<p>Net sales of 1,163,700 tonnes were double the prior week and topped the one-million tonne mark for first time since the week ending October 8, 1992.</p>
<p>Exports of 185,300 tonnes were 23 percent below the previous week and 31 percent below the four-week average.</p>
<p>Primary export destinations: Mexico (45,600), Italy (45,000), Japan (40,200) and Spain (24,000).</p>
</text>
